     snapshot watchers onto each event.
  3. [1mBeing unassigned doesn't unfollow you.[0m Assignment auto-adds you to watchers; only the follow button removes you.

  Also: no-op changes emit no event; toasts cap at three visible with the rest queued; corrupt or unavailable
  [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m degrades to in-memory with a visible banner rather than failing.

  [1mTesting[0m

  The valuable tests are on pure logic, which is most of the risk: the subscription predicate, feed derivation, unread
  counting, no-op suppression, and watcher auto-add. UI gets thin smoke tests. The design deliberately keeps DOM out of
  [38;5;153mevents.js[39m so this is cheap.

  Which brings me to the one thing I do need from you — this repo has no tooling at all, and it's cheapest to decide
  now, before any code exists:
